<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rothenburg ob der Tauber</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rothenburg ob der <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tauber">Tauber</a> is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, above the Tauber valley, which grew below a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> castle and was a free imperial city from 1274 until 1802. Taken by Tilly's imperial army in 1631, it then declined, which preserved its walled medieval townscape, now one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s best-known sights. The festival play of the Master Draught recalls the capture of 1631.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rothenburg-ob-der-tauber.jpg" alt="Rothenburg ob der Tauber" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Berthold Werner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rothenburg_BW_4.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
